5.2 Location-Specific Elements Location-Specific elements can inform the passenger about available infrastructure support and the covered area. This helps the passenger in understanding where the ego-vehicle has information beyond that given by ego sensors. For example, this answers the question “if no traffic is shown on a crossroad, is there really no traffic, or is there just no infrastructure support?” We expect this to positively impact trust because it provides system transparency [45, 78].
